  "theorem_claim": "For a declared pseudometric space, the relation dist x y ≤ epsilon is reflexive for epsilon ≥ 0 and symmetric. Two successive bounds with tolerances epsilon₁ and epsilon₂ imply an endpoint bound epsilon₁+epsilon₂. If a witness chain has both adjacent distances ≤ epsilon but endpoint distance > epsilon, the epsilon-neighborhood relation is not transitive on that domain.",
